Dockerfile
.gradle/
/bin/
/build/
/runtime/

# OPERATOR SECRETS MUST NOT ENTER THE BUILD CONTEXT.
#
# Everything not excluded here is packed up and sent to the Docker daemon on every build - a daemon that
# may be remote, that keeps the context in its own build cache, and whose cache and history any user with
# access to it can read. That happens regardless of what the Dockerfile COPYs, so a file the image never
# contains is still disclosed by building.
#
# Docker Compose reads a '.env' file next to a compose file for its '${...}' interpolation, which is the
# documented way to supply the passwords the examples under docker/examples need (see DOCKER.adoc,
# "Credentials of the compose example"), and '.gitignore' ignores exactly that path so the values stay out
# of the repository. Without the exclusions below the same values would travel to the builder instead.
#
# docker/examples is excluded whole: it is deployment material for an operator, nothing in it is COPYd
# into the image, and it is where a local '.env' lives.
**/.env
**/.env.*
docker/examples/

/themes/common-theme/webapp/common/js/node_modules/
/themes/common-theme/webapp/common-theme/js/node_modules/
/plugins/.svn
/plugins/.github
/plugins/.git
/buildSrc/.gradle
/buildSrc/build
